<concept id="t00582">
	<title>Increasing set speed</title>
	<conbody>
		<table outputclass="formatc_none" frame="none" rowsep="0" colsep="0" id="e03709">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="0">
				<colspec colnum="1" colname="col1" colwidth="2.343*" colsep="0"/>
				<colspec colnum="2" colname="col2" colwidth="2.343*" colsep="0"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="0">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e03710">
								<figgroup>
									<image href="images/N_SP3i25_B10_047_1_IR.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<ul id="e03711">
			<li>
				<p>Push the (+) switch up and release it immediately. The set speed will increase by 1 km/h (1 mph) increments.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>To increase the set speed quickly, push and hold the (+) switch. The set speed will increase in increments of 10. If the cluster speed unit is mph, it will increase in multiples of 5.</p>
				<p>You can set a maximum speed of 180 km/h (110 mph).</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</conbody>
